<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for graph of a system of an absolute value function and a linear function" class="sr-only"><ul><li>For the absolute value function in the system:<br>
<ul>
<li>Moving from left to right:<br>
<ul>
<li>The function slants sharply down to the point (negative 3 comma 4).</li>
<li>The function then slants sharply up.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>The function passes through the following points:<br>
<ul>
<li>(negative seven halves comma nine halves)</li>
<li>(negative 3 comma 4)</li>
<li>(negative five halves comma nine halves)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>For the linear function in the system:<br>
<ul>
<li>The function slants sharply up from left to right.</li>
<li>The function passes through the following points:<br>
<ul>
<li>(negative seven halves comma nine halves)</li>
<li>(0 comma 8)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The graph of a system of an absolute value function and a linear function is shown. What is the solution <math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to this system of two equations?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"45d33d3a-bd12-4475-92e0-96a1fe136db5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 8 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"61dbff2a-9b60-4c6e-a117-8d381756d9bc","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis seven halves comma nine halves right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"8ba6979b-0d9b-4387-b10f-38c4a9dc7c7e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative seven halves comma nine halves right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"b51163fa-59cc-4059-86bf-4fe46a19a631","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 3 comma 4 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["8ba6979b-0d9b-4387-b10f-38c4a9dc7c7e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The solution to a system of two equations corresponds to the point where the graphs of the equations intersect. The graphs of the linear function and the absolute value function shown intersect at a point with an <em>x</em>-coordinate between <math alttext="negative 4"><mrow>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="negative 3"><mrow>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>3</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and a <em>y</em>-coordinate between <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>. Of the given choices, only&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative seven halves comma nine halves right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> has an <em>x</em>-coordinate between <math alttext="negative 4"><mrow>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="negative 3"><mrow>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>3</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and a <em>y</em>-coordinate between <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of the linear function.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the vertex of the graph of the absolute value function.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"494d247d","external_id":"dad4b1da-ac0d-4094-a181-0c9e028aef62","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"e7422617-8b8b-43e1-b805-5e428fe63cd1","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Graph of a system of an absolute value function and a linear function in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from negative 8 to 3. The y axis ranges from 0 to 9. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 286.56 275.22 \nL 286.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 260.46 \nL 279.36 260.46 \nL 279.36 10.98 \nL 7.2 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 10.869179 268.02 \nL 270.020821 268.02 \nL 270.020821 7.2 \nL 10.869179 7.2 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_3\">\n    <g id=\"xtick_1\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_2\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_3\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_4\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_5\"></g>\n   