</mrow>
</math> for the second equation in the given system of equations.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"4fb8a648","external_id":"ba1a8be9-37d7-4a8f-80c3-300f4e67565d","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"94d48cfd-af18-4b08-8645-806afe6b973a","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals x plus 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals x squared plus 16 x plus 63\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>63</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A solution to the given system of equations is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the greatest possible value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f51bd4c8-3d01-41b7-a044-510cd77aae82","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"cadb92c1-969a-4911-9823-c5021b32b732","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e94e7dab-72f3-4271-883b-feb4102548a5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1af731fb-f330-4b9e-beeb-cb0c1302ac9e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"63\"><mn>63</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["f51bd4c8-3d01-41b7-a044-510cd77aae82"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"y equals x plus 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y equals x squared plus 16 x plus 63\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>63</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>; therefore, it follows that <math alttext=\"x plus 9 equals x squared plus 16 x plus 63\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>63</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"x plus 9 equals left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis minus left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis left parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis minus 1 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, <math alttext=\"x plus 9 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> or <math alttext=\"x plus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 9 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the given system of equations has solutions, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, that occur when <math alttext=\"x equals negative 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"x equals negative 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math> is greater than <math alttext=\"negative 9\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</math>, the greatest possible value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the negative of the greatest possible value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> when <math alttext=\"y equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for the second equation in the given system of equations.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> when <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for the first equation in the given system of equations.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> when <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for the second equation in the given system of equations.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357396,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"4fb8a648","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1730147357396,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"ba1a8be9-37d7-4a8f-80c3-300f4e67565d","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"94d48cfd-af18-4b08-8645-806afe6b973a","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"f51bd4c8-3d01-41b7-a044-510cd77aae82"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"cadb92c1-969a-4911-9823-c5021b32b732"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"e94e7dab-72f3-4271-883b-feb4102548a5"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"63\"><mn>63</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"1af731fb-f330-4b9e-beeb-cb0c1302ac9e"}],"externalid":"ba1a8be9-37d7-4a8f-80c3-300f4e67565d","keys":["f51bd4c8-3d01-41b7-a044-510cd77aae82"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"y equals x plus 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y equals x squared plus 16 x plus 63\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>63</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>; therefore, it follows that <math alttext=\"x plus 9 equals x squared plus 16 x plus 63\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>63</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"x plus 9 equals left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis minus left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis left parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis minus 1 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 9 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, <math alttext=\"x plus 9 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> or <math alttext=\"x plus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 9 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the given system of equations has solutions, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, that occur when <math alttext=\"x equals negative 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"x equals negative 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math> is greater than <math alttext=\"negative 9\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn>\n</math>, the greatest possible value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the negative of the greatest possible value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> when <math alttext=\"y equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for the second equation in the given system of equations.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> when <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for the first equation in the given system of equations.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> when <math alttext=\"x equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> for the second equation in the given system of equations.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals x plus 9\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals x squared plus 16 x plus 63\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>63