<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"508344ac","external_id":"e31accbd-71ed-4323-82c0-b30186a84861","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"f310628c-cdcd-47f7-9252-52e9fd1b43b8","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"16 left parenthesis x plus 15 right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f5559ede-7963-4cb9-9ac4-ae4738d440f4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x plus 31\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>31</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d80580e8-4f46-4dff-b60d-e83a4d9d23a4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x plus 240\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>240</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fff86d73-f62a-4903-a899-970e6c95b37c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x plus 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f0b47f0a-7eb4-46a2-bca3-aa566dfb902f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x plus 15\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>15</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["d80580e8-4f46-4dff-b60d-e83a4d9d23a4"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The expression <math alttext=\"16 left parenthesis x plus 15 right parenthesis\"><mn>16</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"16 left parenthesis x right parenthesis plus 16 left parenthesis 15 right parenthesis\"><mn>16</mn><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mfenced><mn>15</mn></mfenced></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"16 x plus 240\"><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>240</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554987,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"508344ac","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1743430554987,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"e31accbd-71ed-4323-82c0-b30186a84861","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"f310628c-cdcd-47f7-9252-52e9fd1b43b8","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"16 left parenthesis x plus 15 right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math>?</p>","keys":["d80580e8-4f46-4dff-b60d-e83a4d9d23a4"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"f5559ede-7963-4cb9-9ac4-ae4738d440f4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x plus 31\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>31</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d80580e8-4f46-4dff-b60d-e83a4d9d23a4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x plus 240\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>240</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fff86d73-f62a-4903-a899-970e6c95b37c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x plus 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f0b47f0a-7eb4-46a2-bca3-aa566dfb902f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x plus 15\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>15</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The expression <math alttext=\"16 left parenthesis x plus 15 right parenthesis\"><mn>16</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"16 left parenthesis x right parenthesis plus 16 left parenthesis 15 right parenthesis\"><mn>16</mn><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mfenced><mn>15</mn></mfenced></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"16 x plus 240\"><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>240</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"e31accbd-71ed-4323-82c0-b30186a84861","correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1743430554987,"updateDate":1743430554987}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554987, 1743430554987),
    ($SATQ$50e40f08$SATQ$, $SATQ$e3e1bd01-4a4e-4c9c-8e91-28a5165667b6$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">If the given function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> is graphed in the <em>xy</em>-plane, where <math alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, what is the <em>x</em>-coordinate of an <em>x</em>-intercept of the graph?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["-6","4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["-6","4"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is either <math alttext="negative 6"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>
</math> or <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math>. The <em>x</em>-intercepts of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane are the points where <math alttext="y equals 0"><mrow>
<mi>y</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Thus, for an <em>x</em>-intercept of the graph of <math alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, <math alttext="0 equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>. Substituting <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> for&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> yields <math alttext="0 equals left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, <math alttext="x plus 6 equals 0"><mrow>
<mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>+</mo>
<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="x minus 4 equals 0"><mrow>
<mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext="x plus 6 equals 0"><mrow>
<mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>+</mo>
<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals negative 6"><mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Adding <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext="x minus 4 equals 0"><mrow>
<mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals 4"><mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the <em>x</em>-coordinates of the <em>x</em>-intercepts of the graph of&nbsp;<math alttext="y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> are <math alttext="negative 6"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math>. Note that -6 and 4 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"50e40f08","external_id":"e3e1bd01-4a4e-4c9c-8e91-28a5165667b6","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"49363232-aa8c-4254-b2d3-a5bdeb17ef81","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the given function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is graphed in the <em>xy</em>-plane, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, what is the <em>x</em>-coordinate of an <em>x</em>-intercept of the graph?</p>","answerOptions":null,"keys":["-6","4"],"correct_answer":["-6","4"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is either <math alttext=\"negative 6\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</math> or <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math>. The <em>x</em>-intercepts of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane are the points where <math alttext=\"y equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mi>y</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Thus, for an <em>x</em>-intercept of the graph of <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, <math alttext=\"0 equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> yields <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, <math alttext=\"x plus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"x minus 4 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 6\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x minus 4 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals 4\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the <em>x</em>-coordinates of the <em>x</em>-intercepts of the graph of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfence